6. DeclarationRef
   declaration → canonical declaration identity
   🟡 CURRENT FRONTIER / P0
══════════════════════════════════

   CORE RESPONSIBILITY:
   Input:  declaration from Stage 5 Name Resolution
   Output: unique, stable DeclarationRef with canonical identity
   NOT:    re-resolving names, re-checking types

   EXAMPLE:
   std.env.args (resolved by Stage 5)
       ↓
   DeclarationRef {
       package_path: "std.env",
       name: "args",
       kind: FUNCTION,
       identity: <canonical>
   }

   COMPLETION CRITERIA (must prove all 4):
   1. Central creation:        DeclarationRef only from canonical producer
   2. Uniqueness:              same declaration → same DeclarationRef
   3. Propagation:             preserved through semantic/type-checking
   4. No string reconstruction: downstream must NOT re-lookup by package+name

   GATE: canonical-declaration-ref-check
   PASS: Identity preserved, propagated, unique
   FAIL: String reconstruction, identity loss, duplication
